extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 105-107 (cache p106-p108, text layer, page_offset +1): the Imperial opens mid-page on printed 105 after the Tsunami, and the Flame Cloud follows on printed 107. The skills, money and kit are the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.''s (printed 97-98, cache p098-p099); printed 101 says the dragon ''borgs have the same O.C.C. skills as the cyborg soldier. Printed 97, 98, 105 and 107 read off 110 dpi renders; every figure agrees with the text layer once the digit cipher is read (!D6xlO+10 = 1D6x10+10, !D6xlOOO = 1D6x1000). || SHARED SKILLS: the five Republic cyborg classes (republic-cyborg-soldier, dragon-borg-wing-blade, dragon-borg-tsunami, dragon-borg-imperial-combat, dragon-borg-flame-cloud) restate ONE skill list, the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.''s (printed 97-98), and MUST BE CHANGED TOGETHER. Printed 101 says the dragon ''borgs have the same O.C.C. skills as the cyborg soldier unless a police officer or mercenary. Identical in all five: O.C.C., related and secondary skills, hand to hand, XP table, starting money, occ_group and men_of_arms, the M.E. requirement, the human-only race restriction and the standard military issue. What differs is the body: the four dragon ''borgs are one class per body (mdc_base, fixed P.S./P.P./Spd, unconditional combat bonuses, weapons and features), following the Free Quebec cyborgs (fq-cyborg-*, BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F31). || XP: the Dragon Borg, Japanese Borg column on the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, printed folio 216), fourth column, bottom block, read off a render: 0 / 2,176 / 4,301 / 8,401 / 17,501 / 24,601 / 36,701 / 44,801 / 57,901 / 94,001 / 130,001 / 190,001 / 240,001 / 280,001 / 330,001. || GROUP: men-of-arms with men_of_arms: true in all five Republic cyborg classes, following fq-cyborg-soldier and cs-cyborg-strike-trooper; the book files the Republic''s cyborgs with no group heading. The soldier states no pool, so the line picks its S.D.C. roll; a dragon ''borg states mdc_base, and the line is kept so the five agree. || BODY AND ATTRIBUTES: main body 350 M.D.C. as mdc_base; the M.D.C. by location, speed and dimensions are the body ability (no vehicles row holds this body). Physical attributes \"equal to a P.S. 30, P.P. 22, Spd 176\" stored as fixed attribute_dice, the ninja-borg, plains-borg and destroyer-borg precedent. Mental attributes and P.B. are the character''s own. Not supersedes_race. The Imperial cannot fly and has no jet thruster; the shared Jet Packs skill is the soldier''s and is kept. || BONUSES: +1 attack per melee, +1 initiative, +1 parry, +2 dodge, +2 pull punch and +2 save vs horror factor stored. The book adds \"plus P.P. 23 bonus of +4 to strike, parry and dodge\" although the body is P.P. 22; the Palladium chart gives +4 at either, and the sheet adds it from the stored P.P. 22, so it is not stored again. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Radio: Basic 45+10, Computer Operation 40+10, Jet Packs 42+20 (printed Pilot Jet Pack), Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10, Find Contraband 26+10 (printed Find Contraband, Weapons & Cybernetics), Land Navigation 36+10, Climbing 40+10, Swimming 50+10. Literacy: Japanese at 98% stored as Literacy: Native Language at the book''s 98, fixed; Language: Japanese 98% as Language: Native Tongue; one language of choice (+15%) as a Language: Other pick. W.P. Heavy Energy Weapons is W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons, as fq-cyborg-soldier stores it. Hand to Hand: Basic Martial Arts/Judo is this book''s row; the upgrade prices (Aikido or Karate one pick, Jujitsu two) are the hand_to_hand block. The Jet Packs figure is the soldier''s +20% in all five; a body''s own bonus to jet pack piloting stays in that body''s prose. || RELATED: five plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. SECONDARY: none at level one; two each at levels 2, 5, 8 and 13, as printed (the FQ soldier''s ninth-level slot is 8 here), from the related list excluding those marked None and without the bonuses. || DEMOLITIONS: printed 107 gives Demolitions and Demolitions Disposal (+10% each) only to those assigned to demolitions; conditional, so an ability and not a grant. || EQUIPMENT: the standard military issue (printed 98), identical in all five Republic cyborg classes: the energy rifle is unspecified, so it is a choice of this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand energy rifles (the stun rifle and the underwater rifle left out); four extra E-clips are the rifle E-clip row; four grenades are a choice of this book''s grenades excluding the armor dissolver, as printed (four of one kind; a mix is the GM''s call); distancing binoculars are infrared-distancing-binoculars; the backpack is pr-1-standard-backpack, this book''s standard pack. The body-styling ammunition, maintenance and repairs are not items, and the jet pack, hover vehicle and extra weapons available upon assignment are not starting kit. The Imperial''s ammunition, missiles and gas canisters are its own systems and prose. || MONEY: monthly salary 2,000 credits (officers of 9th level and up 3,500 to 5,000; police ''borgs 800 more than an unaugmented officer); starting_money holds the 1D6x1000 the book gives as a first-level character''s savings. Room, board, clothing and medical care are provided. The text layer ciphers the savings as !D6xlOOO. || INSANITY: the Tsunami''s rule (printed 103) with the Imperial''s 5% first year, +2% per year; prose in side_effects."
