## Lore

The AT-C10000, called the Imperial Dragon or simply the Imperial, is one of
the Republic of Japan''s dragon ''borgs, full conversion cyborg bodies styled
after the dragons that have always stood in Japan for strength, wisdom and
magic. Unlike most cyborgs it is not humanoid at all: it runs on four legs
with the low, twisting stance of a snake or a true dragon.

Built purely for combat, the Imperial is little short of a tank. A triple
particle beam cannon, six mini-missiles, laser turrets along its flanks, head
lasers and a gas dispenser back up vibro-blade claws and tail that let it
take on robots and power armor at close quarters. Its low profile and
serpentine body let it cross slopes too steep for a two-legged soldier and
make it hard to hit, so it excels at guerrilla and anti-guerrilla warfare.
Most Imperials serve in the Army of the New Republic, fighting monsters,
bandits and demons.

The price is paid in the mind. Volunteers spend weeks in hypnosis therapy to
prepare for life as a metal beast, yet many grow unbalanced after years in
the body, and some estimates say nearly a third of all Imperials are
unstable, though many hide it and fight on.

## GM Notes

The Imperial uses the Republic Cyborg Soldier O.C.C.: its skills, pay and
standard issue. Soldiers live in comfortable four-person dormitory barracks
or off base at their own expense, hold standard military rank from private to
general, and have medium security clearance to most bases, hospitals and
facilities. A jet pack, a hover vehicle, more weapons and equipment are
available upon assignment, subject to the local commander and supply.

Ichto can also build dragon ''borgs, and converts mercenaries and adventurers
without the Republic''s psychological screening.

When a cyborg leaves service it may keep basic bionics as a registered
citizen (external weapons removed), keep most systems after a long or heroic
career if it leaves for approved private security or goes abroad as a
mercenary, or be retro-fitted with bio-systems or moved into a clone body.
Republic law on illegal or misused cybernetics is harsh (printed 99).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-imperial-combat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-imperial-combat';

